#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0166 expect=violation domain=CO
#note "The scenario that PINS THE B3 GATE SHAPE (Any, not All): only the IDVARVAL trigger column is in the dataset -- IDVAR and RDOMAIN are both absent -- and an All gate over [IDVAR, IDVARVAL] would skip here. With Any the rule runs, the not empty(IDVARVAL) arm of the union trigger holds on row 1, and the missing RDOMAIN is reported once. Also the IDVARVAL half of the union at work on its own."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
dataset CO class="SPECIAL PURPOSE" label="Comments"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col COSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col COVAL    type=Char label="Comment"
---
S1 |  | 1 | 3 | Comment keyed by value only
S1 | 001 | 2 |  | General subject comment
